% A test of constants that reads more than a quantum before it holds still
% lets the rule reach what it reads next.  Without an index, q(19999, _)
% is checked by reading q until a tuple holds, and q's 20000 tuples are
% derived with 19999, every digit at its last fact, the last of them, so
% the check reads all of q.  Every thread count derives v's 100 values.
e(0).
e(1).
d(0).
d(1).
d(2).
d(3).
d(4).
d(5).
d(6).
d(7).
d(8).
d(9).
q(N, N) :- e(A), d(B), d(C), d(D), d(E),
    N = A * 10000 + B * 1000 + C * 100 + D * 10 + E.
v(X) :- d(A), d(B), X = A * 10 + B.
p(X) :- q(19999, _), v(X).

p(X)?
